    terms: [
      { id: "operator", title: "1. Nature of this website", text: "Heptapus Group is a project/brand, not currently presented as an incorporated company. Project and service descriptions are informational. This website does not automatically create a sale, payment or service agreement. Any separate service agreement must identify its parties and define scope, price, delivery, rights and responsibilities." },
      { id: "use", title: "2. Appropriate use", text: "Use this site lawfully for information and enquiries. Unauthorised access, account sharing, harmful files, spam, impersonation and service disruption are prohibited. Administration is restricted to authorised accounts; public registration is closed. Protect account/device access and report suspicious activity." },
      { id: "content", title: "3. Content and intellectual property", text: "Rights in original text, software, images and brands remain with their respective owners. Links or third-party marks do not transfer those rights. Statutory exceptions and permitted quotation remain available; obtain permission for other uses. You must have authority to share content submitted through forms." },
      { id: "external", title: "4. External services and availability", text: "External sites/players have their own terms. Maintenance, networks and providers may cause interruptions; project descriptions may change. No unlimited guarantee of results or availability is offered. Nothing here excludes mandatory rights or liability that cannot lawfully be limited." },
      { id: "privacy", title: "5. Data and contact", text: `Data processing is described in the data protection, privacy and cookie notices. Reading terms is not consent. Contact ${email} for enquiries or rights requests. Do not submit others' data without authority or unnecessary sensitive information.` },
      { id: "updates", title: "6. Updates and applicable rights", text: "The page shows its version. An updated notice does not expand existing consent automatically. Separate contracts and mandatory law remain applicable. This page does not impose exclusive court jurisdiction or broad waivers without identifying the parties and legal relationship." },
    ],
